{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>When you beget.</b> That is, when you will say, 'We have already settled in the land,' and He will no longer increase anger and destruction — I testify upon you with things that endure forever, namely heaven and earth, that כי אבוד תאבדון, and what will avail you is nothing, that you settled in it. Another interpretation: our Rabbis of blessed memory explained: if you are in the land like the count of ונושנתם — אבוד תאבדון. And the Holy One, blessed be He, did righteousness for us, that He advanced the destruction two years before the count of ונושנתם. As it is said: וישקוד ה׳ על הרעה ויביא׳ עלינו, כי צדיק ה׳ אלהינו."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:29.093465791Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}